list.item:
its bounds, always where they can be given, in TEI's attributes, as years of four digits
        (0813), months (0816-08) or days (0813-06-13):


a point known to its precision: when;

a point somewhere between two dates: notBefore and notAfter;

a span, such as a bishop's years or an owner's: from and to;

its EDTF, where the bounds can't say what the words do: in when-custom for a point,
        in from-custom and to-custom for a span's ends, with datingMethod pointing
        to the file's declaration of EDTF, #edtf (). EDTF says:


circa, by ~ (0800~), uncertain, by ? (0756?), or
            both, by %;

a century as the interval of its years (0801/0900), and a part of one as its own
            (0867/0900);

a decade by unspecified digits (081X);

a point among a few dates, by a set ([0755,0756]).

the bounds agree with the EDTF, by years: an exact date, an interval and a date with unspecified
        digits have the bounds' years exactly, so that 09XX goes with 900 to 999; a circa or uncertain
        one lies within the bounds (a warning);
